cts/opencomputer\",\n    31→    \"description\": \"The easiest way to deploy a managed AI agent. Describe what your agent should do, paste one prompt into your coding agent, and get a live agent URL. Agents are always-on, steerable mid-run, and accessible via a permanent URL — designed for developers building with AI coding agents.\",\n    32→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-25\",\n    33→    \"category\": \"code agent\",\n    34→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    35→    \"community_quotes\": [\n    36→      \"The easiest way to deploy a managed agent — say what your agent should do, paste one prompt, get a live agent URL.\",\n    37→      \"Agents are always-on, steerable mid-run, and accessible via a permanent URL.\",\n    38→      \"216 votes on the Product Hunt weekly leaderboard for July 20, 2026.\"\n    39→    ]\n    40→  },\n    41→  {\n    42→    \"name\": \"Velane\",\n    43→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/velane\",\n    44→    \"description\": \"A cloud platform purpose-built for managing AI agents' tools and functions, providing a code sandbox, 800+ integrations, and version control. Designed to be agent-first and fully controlled by AI agents like Claude and Codex, serving as the tooling layer for agentic coding workflows.\",\n    45→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-25\",\n    46→    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    47→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    48→    \"community_quotes\": [\n    49→      \"Cloud for your AI Agent's tools and functions — agent first, and fully controlled by your AI Agent.\",\n    50→      \"Provides a code sandbox, 800+ integrations, and version control for agent-managed tooling.\",\n    51→      \"A cloud layer designed to manage the tools and functions that an AI agent uses.\"\n    52→    ]\n    53→  },\n    54→  {\n    55→    \"name\": \"OpenCode Superapp\",\n    56→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/opencode-superapp\",\n    57→    \"description\": \"A native workspace that gives developers the power of Codex with local, self-hosted models and voice. Agents understand your projects, work with files, Git, and terminals, and speak with you through voice — supporting cloud, local, or self-hosted model providers.\",\n    58→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-26\",\n    59→    \"category\": \"AI IDE\",\n    60→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    61→    \"community_quotes\": [\n    62→      \"The power of Codex with local, self-hosted models and voice.\",\n    63→      \"Run cloud, local, or self-hosted models in a native workspace where agents understand your projects.\",\n    64→      \"Combines Codex-like power with local, self-hosted AI and voice for a complete coding agent experience.\"\n    65→    ]\n    66→  },\n    67→  {\n    68→    \"name\": \"Caider\",\n    69→    \"url\": \"https://caider.dev\",\n    70→    \"description\": \"A Mac app that turns your computer into a hands-off coding agent bridging GitHub issues and local AI execution. It automatically resolves GitHub issues into merged pull requests using your local AI agents (Claude, Antigravity), keeping all code on your machine for privacy.\",\n    71→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-26\",\n    72→    \"category\": \"code agent\",\n    73→    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    74→    \"community_quotes\": [\n    75→      \"From GitHub issue to merged PR — approve from anywhere, execution runs on your own Mac.\",\n    76→      \"Lets you stay in GitHub issues interface while using your local AI agents to code on them.\",\n    77→      \"Your code never leaves your machine — complete context on development including back-and-forth research with AI agent.\"\n    78→    ]\n    79→  },\n    80→  {\n    81→    \"name\": \"FluentDB\",\n    82→    \"url\": \"https://www.fluentdb.ai\",\n    83→    \"description\": \"A native macOS database client with an AI co-pilot that lets developers explore and query PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, and SQL Server. Users can ask questions in plain English and get reliable SQL back, designed as an AI-first experience for developers working with databases.\",\n    84→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-25\",\n    85→    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n    86→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    87→    \"community_quotes\": [\n    88→      \"The AI database app built for Mac — fast, delightful, secure, and AI-first.\",\n    89→      \"Explore and query PostgreSQL, MySQL, and SQLite, ask questions in plain English, and get SQL you can trust.\"\n    90→    ]\n    91→  },\n    92→  {\n    93→    \"name\": \"Cosyra 2.0\",\n    94→    \"url\": \"https://cosyra.com\",\n    95→    \"description\": \"A persistent Linux cloud workspace tailored for running AI coding agents directly from a mobile phone. Run Claude Code, Codex CLI, and Gemini CLI in a cloud container without managing your own VPS — agents keep running in the background without needing to keep a device awake.\",\n    96→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-23\",\n    97→    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    98→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n    99→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   100→      \"A persistent Linux workspace for coding agents on your phone.\",\n   101→      \"Run Claude Code or Codex CLI on your phone from a cloud Ubuntu terminal without managing your own VPS.\",\n   102→      \"Cloud workspace for coding agents — manage code repositories, branches, and more from anywhere.\"\n   103→    ]\n   104→  },\n   105→  {\n   106→    \"name\": \"ditto.site\",\n   107→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/ion-design/ditto.site\",\n   108→    \"description\": \"A free, open-source tool that clones any live website by URL and outputs clean, production-ready TypeScript / Next.js code with components, design tokens, interactions, and hover effects. Turns a public URL into a self-contained Next.js app by capturing what the browser actually rendered.\",\n   109→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-21\",\n   110→    \"category\": \"open-source dev tool\",\n   111→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\", \"GitHub\"],\n   112→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   113→      \"Clone any website into clean code — free and open source.\",\n   114→      \"#3 Product of the Day on Product Hunt with 648 followers.\",\n   115→      \"Turns any live site into clean, production-ready code with components, design tokens, interactions, and hover effects.\"\n   116→    ]\n   117→  },\n   118→  {\n   119→    \"name\": \"Kastra\",\n   120→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/kastra\",\n   121→    \"description\": \"A runtime authorization layer for AI coding agents including Claude, Cursor, Codex, and OpenClaw. Provides security and access controls specifically designed for agentic coding workflows, ensuring coding agents operate with proper permissions guardrails.\",\n   122→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n   123→    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n   124→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n   125→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   126→      \"Runtime authorization for Claude, Cursor, Codex and OpenClaw.\",\n   127→      \"Featured on the Product Hunt weekly leaderboard for July 20, 2026.\",\n   128→      \"Provides a security and authorization layer specifically for agentic coding workflows.\"\n   129→    ]\n   130→  },\n   131→  {\n   132→    \"name\": \"tterm\",\n   133→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/tterm\",\n   134→    \"description\": \"A unified workspace combining a terminal, browser, and Claude Code under one roof, designed for developers who want to manage their AI coding agent workflows from a single interface. Bridges terminal-based coding agent work with browser-based tasks.\",\n   135→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-22\",\n   136→    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n   137→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n   138→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   139→      \"Terminal, browser, and Claude Code under one roof.\",\n   140→      \"A unified workspace for managing AI coding agent workflows from a single interface.\"\n   141→    ]\n   142→  },\n   143→  {\n   144→    \"name\": \"Forall\",\n   145→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/astrio-labs/forall\",\n   146→    \"description\": \"An open-source AI coding agent that generates spec-driven code alongside machine-checkable proofs. Built for developers who need formally verified software, it produces code and proofs in languages like Lean and Dafny, ensuring correctness through mathematical verification rather than just AI-generated output.\",\n   147→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-20\",\n   148→    \"category\": \"open-source code agent\",\n   149→    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n   150→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   151→      \"An AI coding agent that generates machine-checkable proofs — spec-driven code with formal verification.\",\n   152→      \"Open-source coding agent from Astrio that helps developers build correct software.\",\n   153→      \"Currently supports 3 verifiable languages, with interest from the formal verification community.\"\n   154→    ]\n   155→  },\n   156→  {\n   157→    \"name\": \"Clark\",\n   158→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/clark-agent\",\n   159→    \"description\": \"An AI coworker with its own cloud computer featuring a browser, terminal, files, and code execution. Users can hand it a real engineering task, close the tab, and return to completed work, positioning it as an autonomous coding and task-execution agent rather than a chat assistant.\",\n   160→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-18\",\n   161→    \"category\": \"code agent\",\n   162→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n   163→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   164→      \"Clark is an AI coworker that runs inside its own cloud computer. The pitch is less about conversation than execution.\",\n   165→      \"5.0 rating across 908 reviews on Product Hunt — extremely positive reception.\",\n   166→      \"Differentiated from chat-based AI by emphasizing execution — actually performing tasks via its own cloud computer.\"\n   167→    ]\n   168→  },\n   169→  {\n   170→    \"name\": \"Unabyss for Claude\",\n   171→    \"url\": \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/unabyss\",\n   172→    \"description\": \"An MCP-native self-updating context and memory layer that gives Claude shared memory across apps, agents, and LLMs. It syncs context across Claude, GPT, and Cursor, with stale-context conflict resolution, specifically designed to enhance coding assistant workflows with persistent project memory.\",\n   173→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-17\",\n   174→    \"category\": \"workflow agent\",\n   175→    \"sources\": [\"Product Hunt\"],\n   176→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   177→      \"#1 Product of the Day on Product Hunt for July 17, 2026.\",\n   178→      \"Gives Claude workflows shared memory across apps, agents, and LLMs with stale-context conflict resolution.\",\n   179→      \"Two ways to supercharge your coding assistant — Codex Micro vs Unabyss for Claude were the standout launches that week.\"\n   180→    ]\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"name\": \"Juggler\",\n   184→    \"url\": \"https://github.com/juggler-ai/juggler\",\n   185→    \"description\": \"An open-source GUI-based AI coding agent providing a visual workbench with inspectable tool calls, branching threads, and editable context. Built in Go with Wails, using Yjs CRDT documents for session management and a Miller-column interface for navigating agent interactions.\",\n   186→    \"release_date\": \"2026-07-14\",\n   187→    \"category\": \"open-source code agent\",\n   188→    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n   189→    \"community_quotes\": [\n   190→      \"278 points and 118 comments on Hacker News — strong community interest.\",\n   191→      \"Surprisingly, I've really enjoyed the experience of using Juggler for coding tasks.\",\n   192→      \"Another AI coding agent, but the visual workbench with inspectable tool calls and branching threads sets it apart.\",\n   193→      \"Created by Julian Storer, the renowned developer behind the JUCE C++ framework — brings credibility from the audio/C++ world.\"\n   194→    ]\n   195→  }\n   196→]\n   197→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
