          "+        <!-- Devin July 24 -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Devin</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin (July 24): Redesigned model picker, slash commands, OIDC tokens</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Unified model picker, discoverable slash commands (/btw, /queue, /ask), playbook previews, Windows sessions from Slack via !windows, approve/deny network access from Slack, OIDC identity tokens for cloud auth, and API additions for code scans.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-24</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Devin Outposts -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Devin</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://devin.ai/blog/introducing-devin-outposts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Introducing Devin Outposts: Run Devin Cloud on any machine you operate</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Devin Cloud sessions can now run on any user-operated machine — GPU boxes, VMs, Kubernetes clusters, or local hardware. Named queues with workers that only dial out. Partners include Namespace, Cloudflare, Modal, NVIDIA Brev, Daytona, E2B.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip positive\">+ \"89% of all code at Cognition now written by Devin\"</span>",
          "             </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#boris-cherny\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Opus 5 improved vulnerability finding but not exploitation</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Least prompt-injectable model yet from Anthropic. Close to Mythos 5 at finding vulnerabilities but substantially behind on exploitation. Improved as a side effect of general capability gains.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Boris Cherny / Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-25</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                    <span class=\"topic\">AI security</span><span class=\"topic\">prompt injection</span><span class=\"topic\">red teaming</span>",
          "-                </div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Copilot Gemini 3.6 Flash -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">GitHub Copilot</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-21-gemini-3-6-flash-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini 3.6 Flash added to GitHub Copilot</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Available for web/app development, coding, and longer-horizon agentic tasks with configurable reasoning effort and parallel tool use. Copilot Pro and higher across 8 environments. Follows deprecation of Gemini 2.5 Pro and Gemini 3 Flash.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip positive\">+ \"3.6 Flash is a really really good model for code\"</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#ruff-v016\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ruff v0.16.0 ships 413 default rules&mdash;AI-assisted auto-fix</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Astral shipped Ruff with 413 rules (up from 59). Willison used Codex (GPT-5.6 Sol) and Claude Code (Opus 5) to auto-fix hundreds of issues across Datasette, sqlite-utils, and LLM.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-25</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                    <span class=\"topic\">Ruff</span><span class=\"topic\">Python</span><span class=\"topic\">AI-assisted</span>",
          "-                </div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Cursor Agent Swarms -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Cursor</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/agent-swarm-model-economics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Agent Swarms: AI agents autonomously rebuild SQLite from spec in Rust</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">A swarm of AI agents rebuilt SQLite from its 835-page spec into Rust, passing 100% of a held-out test suite. The hierarchical architecture reached ~1,000 commits/hour and reduced costs ~8x from $10,565 to $1,339/run using Opus 4.8 planner + Composer 2.5 workers.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip positive\">+ 8x cost reduction at 100% test pass rate</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip neutral\">~ \"The only models trusted autonomously cost more than a human\"</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus 5 launched&mdash;1M context, step-change improvement</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">$5/M input, $25/M output. Wrote its own computer vision pipeline to reconstruct a 3D FreeCAD model from raw pixel data when denied direct image access. Available in Copilot on launch day.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Anthropic &middot; 2026-07-24</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"topics\">",
          "-                    <span class=\"topic\">Claude Opus 5</span><span class=\"topic\">1M context</span>",
          "-                </div>",
          "-            </article>",
