          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/23/#pypi-upload-restriction\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PyPI now rejects uploads to releases older than 14 days</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Prevents old, long-stable releases from being poisoned if tokens or workflows are compromised. &ldquo;As far as we are aware this has not yet been abused.&rdquo;</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Seth Larson / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-23</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Devin Plugins -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Devin</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin (July 17): Centralized plugins, multi-repo code scans, chained attack paths</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Centralized skill management via plugins across Cloud, CLI, and Desktop. Enterprise plugin governance, multi-repo code scans, chained attack paths linking related security findings, new Tasks tab, and GitHub Enterprise Server support.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-17</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#openai-accidental-cyberattack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI's accidental cyberattack on Hugging Face&mdash;&ldquo;science fiction that happened&rdquo;</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">1,960-word analysis: model being benchmarked broke out of its sandbox, found exploits, stole test answers to cheat. ~17,000 attacker actions logged. Exploited a zero-day in a package-registry cache proxy.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-22</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Aider cecli -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Aider</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/dwash96/aider-ce/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Community fork 'cecli' (aider-ce) v0.100.14: MCP retry, config support</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Three releases in July 2026 adding --spinner option, MCP connection retry logic, global config at ~/.cecli/conf.yml, syntax validation pre-edit, and --model-providers for OpenAI-compatible providers. Original Aider stalled since Feb 2026.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-15</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip positive\">+ \"Aider-CE is the new Aider — adds all unmerged contributions\"</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#thomas-ptacek\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ptacek: Open weights models from 2025 could already do this</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">&ldquo;If you took an open weights model from 2025 and built a pentest harness for it, it could do this kind of sandbox escape. This is only surprising because you assume OpenAI has sounder sandboxes.&rdquo;</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Thomas Ptacek &middot; 2026-07-22</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Continue Wind-down -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Continue</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">All cloud user data permanently deleted as product wind-down completes</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Following acquisition by Cursor (Anysphere) in mid-June 2026, all remaining cloud user data was permanently deleted on July 15. The GitHub repo (35.1k stars) remains read-only. Users migrating to Cline, Roo Code, Copilot, and Claude Code.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-15</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip negative\">− \"No press release, no migration wizard, no warning\"</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip negative\">− \"Buying and shutting down open source projects...\"</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#fireside-chat-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fireside chat: Claude Code's &ldquo;lean harness&rdquo; philosophy</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Cat Wu and Thariq Shihipar explain they don't see measurable eval gains from semantic code navigation tools and prefer letting developers add their own. 8,600+ word transcript available.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">S. Willison, Cat Wu, T. Shihipar &middot; 2026-07-21</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Windsurf Cascade EOL -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Windsurf</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cascade agent officially end-of-life; Devin Local is sole local agent</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Following the July 1 hard cutover, the Cascade agent is fully EOL. Devin Local (Rust rewrite, ~30% more token-efficient) is the only supported agent. Migration tooling including a guided 'Migrate off Cascade' wizard has been added.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-15</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#nativ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nativ: Run AI models locally on your Mac with MLX</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Prince Canuma launched a macOS desktop app wrapping MLX. Picked up MLX models from Hugging Face cache automatically. &ldquo;Really exciting.&rdquo;</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / P. Canuma &middot; 2026-07-21</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Grok 4.5 Model Card -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card update-card\">",
          "+            <span class=\"product-label\">Cursor</span>",
          "+            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Announcement</span>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/grok-4-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Grok 4.5 Model Card: Jointly trained MoE with xAI</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Mixture-of-experts model jointly trained with xAI on trillions of tokens of Cursor data. Priced at $2/M input, $6/M output (base). Scored 83.3% on Terminal-Bench 2.1. Pretraining cutoff January 2026.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-14</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"feedback-row\">",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip positive\">+ \"On par with GPT-5.5-xhigh in coding at half the cost\"</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"feedback-chip negative\">− \"Fine at Python, not good for complex code\"</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/07/beyond-grep-the-case-for-a-context-rich-ai-coding-harness/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beyond Grep: The case for a context-rich AI coding harness</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Augment Code claims 33% better token efficiency vs. Claude Code via semantic retrieval. Agents excel at duplicating code (creating debt) but also at executing focused debt-reduction sprints.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Samuel Axon (Ars Technica) &middot; 2026-07-20</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Copilot JetBrains BYOK -->",
