          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#ai-mania-eviscerating\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Mania is eviscerating global decision-making</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Nik Suresh's scathing report: an exec who'd never used ChatGPT produced an entirely AI-centric strategy; vendors must validate absurd 100x productivity claims or risk losing contracts.</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Nik Suresh / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-19</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- LLM Relay Market -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Matt Lenhard / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/26/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Inside the Relay Market Powering LLM Token Resellers and Fraud</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Investigation reveals a shadow economy of LLM API token resellers. Relay services intercept API calls enabling unauthorized reselling, rate limit evasion, and fraud — posing risks to providers and end users.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">LLM API</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">fraud</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">infrastructure</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-26</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-            <article class=\"insight-item\">",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#bun-rust-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code uses Rust-ported Bun v1.4.0 in production across millions of devices</a></div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-desc\">563 Rust source files found in the Claude binary. 10% faster startup on Linux. Jarred Sumner: &ldquo;barely anyone noticed. Boring is good.&rdquo;</div>",
          "-                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / J. Sumner &middot; 2026-07-19</div>",
          "-            </article>",
          "+        <!-- Opus 5 Vulnerability Finding -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Boris Cherny / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#boris-cherny\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus 5: Improved Vulnerability Finding But Not Exploitation</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Opus 5 is the least prompt-injectable model yet from Anthropic. Comes close to Mythos 5 at finding vulnerabilities but remains substantially behind on exploitation. Improved as a side effect of general capability gains.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">security</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">prompt injection</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">red teaming</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-25</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          " ",
          "-        </section>",
          "+        <!-- Ruff v0.16.0 -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#ruff-v016\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ruff v0.16.0 Ships 413 Default Rules — Fixed with Claude Code and Codex</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Astral shipped Ruff with 413 rules enabled by default (up from 59). Willison used Codex (GPT-5.6 Sol) for LLM/sqlite-utils and Claude Code (Opus 5) for Datasette — demonstrating real-world AI-assisted code maintenance.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">Ruff</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">Python</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">linting</span>",
          "+            </div>",
