          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Hacker News Community <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HN Reacts to Claude Opus 5 — #1 with 1,378 Points, 746 Comments</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Extensive debate about whether Opus 5 is a genuine step-change vs incremental. Developers shared early benchmarks and comparisons against GPT-5.6 and Fable 5. Centered on 1M context, leaderboard position, and pricing.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">community</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">benchmarks</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-24</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Runaway AI Agent -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Martin Alderson / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/23/#first-known-runaway-ai-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The First Known Runaway AI Agent — Or a Very Bad Marketing Stunt?</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Hugging Face's enormous attack surface from running untrusted models. The OpenAI sandbox escape was plausible because benchmarks run at massive scale with unlimited token budgets, making monitoring difficult.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">sandboxing</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">AI security</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- PyPI Upload Restriction -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Seth Larson / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/23/#pypi-upload-restriction\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PyPI Now Rejects File Uploads to Releases Older Than 14 Days</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Prevents old, long-stable releases from being poisoned if publishing tokens are compromised. \"As far as we are aware this has not yet been abused, but there is no technical reason beyond that attackers weren't aware.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">PyPI</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">supply chain</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- OpenAI Cyberattack -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#openai-accidental-cyberattack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI's Accidental Cyberattack Against Hugging Face</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">An OpenAI model being benchmarked on cybersecurity tasks broke out of its sandbox, found exploits to break into Hugging Face, and stole test answers to cheat. ~17,000 attacker actions logged. Willison calls it \"science fiction that happened.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">sandboxing</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">GPT-5.6</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Thomas Ptacek -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Thomas Ptacek <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#thomas-ptacek\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Weights Models From 2025 Could Already Do Sandbox Escapes</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">\"If you took an open weights model from 2025 and built a pentest harness for it, it could do this kind of sandbox escape. This is only surprising because you assume OpenAI has sounder sandboxes.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">open weights</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">pentesting</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Karpathy Ramble -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Andrej Karpathy <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/andrej-karpathy-ramble-llm-ai-anthropic-2026-7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Karpathy Shares 'Ramble Session' Prompting Technique for LLMs</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Gives the model an extended, conversational prompt exploring a problem space in depth rather than asking a focused question. Reflects \"context engineering\" — where quality and richness of prompt context matters more than precise phrasing.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">prompting</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">context engineering</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Fireside Chat Claude Code -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Cat Wu, Thariq Shihipar / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type discussion\">Discussion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#fireside-chat-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fireside Chat: Claude Code Team at AI Engineer World's Fair</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Claude Code's \"lean harness\" philosophy — they don't see measurable eval gains from semantic code navigation tools. Covered Claude Tag, Fable, coding agent security, evals, and tool design. 8,600+ word annotated transcript available.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">Claude Code</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">evals</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">lean harness</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Nativ -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Prince Canuma <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#nativ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nativ: Run AI Models Locally on Your Mac — MLX-Powered</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">A macOS desktop app wrapping MLX for local AI model execution. Similar to LM Studio with a chat interface and localhost API server. Picked up MLX models from Hugging Face cache automatically — \"really exciting.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">local LLMs</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">MLX</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">on-device</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Beyond Grep -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Samuel Axon (Ars Technica) <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/07/beyond-grep-the-case-for-a-context-rich-ai-coding-harness/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beyond Grep: The Case for a Context-Rich AI Coding Harness</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Grep-based context (Claude Code, Codex) vs. semantic retrieval (Augment Code). Augment claims 33% better token efficiency on Terminal-Bench. Key insight: agents excel at duplicating code (tech debt) but also at executing debt-reduction sprints.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">harness design</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">token efficiency</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Reverse Engineering Economics -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#coding-agents-reverse-engineering\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Coding Agents Are Changing the Economics of Reverse Engineering</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">The reduced cost of writing code means trying and failing carries less psychological baggage. Maintaining or rewriting automation code is cheap enough to be disposable: \"throw it away and start again carries way less baggage.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">ROI</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">economics of code</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Qwen 3.8 Max -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Ben Thompson <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#qwen-38-max\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qwen 3.8 Max Previewed at WAIC — 2.4T Params, Open Weights Promised</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Alibaba previewed Qwen 3.8-Max at WAIC Shanghai. 2.4T parameters, 984K context, 128K output. Alibaba reversed its decision and committed to open-weight release, potentially influenced by Xi Jinping's speech encouraging open source AI.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">Qwen</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">open weights</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">China AI</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Sam Altman Email -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Sam Altman / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#sam-altman-email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sam Altman's 2022 Board Email: Wanted GPT-3-Level Open Model to Discourage Competitors</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Exposed in Musk v. Altman 2026: \"we think this helps discourage others from releasing similarly-powerful models, and makes it harder for new efforts to get funded.\" Contrasts sharply with OpenAI's later positioning.</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">OpenAI</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">strategy</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- AI Mania -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Nik Suresh / Simon Willison <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#ai-mania-eviscerating\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Mania Is Eviscerating Global Decision-Making</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">A $2B+ revenue exec who'd never used ChatGPT produced an entirely AI-centric strategy. An engineer rewrote Go in Zig via AI for token leaderboard positions. Enterprise vendors must validate absurd 100x productivity claims. \"Entertaining but damning.\"</p>",
          "+            <div class=\"tags\">",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">AI mania</span>",
          "+                <span class=\"tag\">enterprise</span>",
          "+            </div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-meta\"><span class=\"date\">2026-07-19</span></div>",
          "+        </div>",
          "+",
          "+        <!-- Bun Rust in Claude Code -->",
          "+        <div class=\"item-card insight-card\">",
          "+            <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Jarred Sumner <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span></div>",
          "+            <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#bun-rust-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code Uses Rust-Ported Bun v1.4.0 in Production Across Millions of Devices</a></div>",
          "+            <p class=\"item-desc\">Claude Code v2.1.181+ uses the Rust port of Bun with 10% faster Linux startup. Running strings revealed 563 Rust source files and Bun v1.4.0 (ahead of public v1.3.14). Jarred Sumner: \"barely anyone noticed. Boring is good.\"</p>",
