    "originalFile": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-07-26</title>\n    <style>\n        /* ===== Reset & Base ===== */\n        *, *::before, *::after {\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n        }\n\n        :root {\n            --bg: #f6f6ef;\n            --text-primary: #000000;\n            --text-secondary: #828282;\n            --accent: #ff6600;\n            --accent-light: #ff9055;\n            --border: #d4d4d4;\n            --border-light: #e8e8e0;\n            --card-bg: #ffffff;\n            --tag-bg: #f0f0e8;\n            --positive: #3a9130;\n            --negative: #c0392b;\n            --code-bg: #f0f0e8;\n        }\n\n        html {\n            font-size: 14px;\n            scroll-behavior: smooth;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            background-color: var(--bg);\n            color: var(--text-primary);\n            line-height: 1.5;\n            min-height: 100vh;\n        }\n\n        a {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            text-decoration: none;\n            transition: color 0.15s ease;\n        }\n\n        a:hover {\n            color: var(--accent-light);\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        code {\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            background-color: var(--code-bg);\n            padding: 1px 4px;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Header ===== */\n        header.site-header {\n            background-color: var(--accent);\n            padding: 6px 16px;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 10px;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n        }\n\n        header.site-header h1 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 1.15rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #fff;\n            margin-right: auto;\n        }\n\n        header.site-header .header-nav a {\n            color: #fff;\n            font-size: 0.8rem;\n            margin-left: 12px;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        header.site-header .header-nav a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Sub-Header ===== */\n        .sub-header {\n            background-color: var(--bg);\n            padding: 16px 20px 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);\n        }\n\n        .sub-header h2 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 1.6rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: var(--text-primary);\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .sub-header .meta-info {\n            font-size: 0.78rem;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 16px;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n        }\n\n        .sub-header .meta-info span {\n            display: inline-flex;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .sub-header .meta-info .dot {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            margin-right: 4px;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Main Layout ===== */\n        main.layout {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 0;\n            max-width: 100%;\n            padding: 0;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Columns ===== */\n        .column {\n            padding: 16px 14px;\n            border-right: 1px solid var(--border-light);\n            min-width: 0;\n        }\n\n        .column:last-child {\n            border-right: none;\n        }\n\n        .column-header {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 0.82rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            letter-spacing: 0.04em;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n            padding-bottom: 8px;\n            margin-bottom: 14px;\n            border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: baseline;\n        }\n\n        .column-header .count {\n            font-size: 0.7rem;\n            background-color: var(--tag-bg);\n            padding: 1px 7px;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n            letter-spacing: 0;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Item Cards ===== */\n        .item {\n            margin-bottom: 16px;\n            padding: 10px 12px;\n            background-color: var(--card-bg);\n            border: 1px solid var(--border-light);\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            transition: box-shadow 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;\n        }\n\n        .item:hover {\n            border-color: var(--border);\n            box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);\n        }\n\n        .item:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .item-title {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 0.9rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n            line-height: 1.35;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a {\n            color: var(--text-primary);\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:hover {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .item-desc {\n            font-size: 0.78rem;\n            color: #333;\n            margin-bottom: 6px;\n            line-height: 1.45;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta {\n            font-size: 0.7rem;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n            display: flex;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            gap: 6px 10px;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta .tag {\n            background-color: var(--tag-bg);\n            padding: 1px 6px;\n            border-radius: 3px;\n            color: #555;\n            font-size: 0.68rem;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta .tag.cat {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta .source {\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta .date {\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n            font-size: 0.68rem;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta .spacer {\n            color: var(--border);\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Community Feedback ===== */\n        .feedback {\n            margin-top: 8px;\n            padding: 6px 8px;\n            border-left: 3px solid var(--border);\n            background-color: #fafaf6;\n            font-size: 0.72rem;\n            color: #555;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote {\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote:last-child {\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote-source {\n            font-style: normal;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n            font-size: 0.66rem;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote.positive {\n            border-left: none;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote.negative {\n            border-left: none;\n            color: #8a3a32;\n        }\n\n        .feedback .quote.neutral {\n            border-left: none;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Update Type Badges ===== */\n        .badge {\n            display: inline-block;\n            font-size: 0.62rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            padding: 1px 5px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            letter-spacing: 0.03em;\n        }\n\n        .badge.release { background-color: #e6f5e6; color: var(--positive); }\n        .badge.feature { background-color: #e6f0fa; color: #2660c0; }\n        .badge.announcement { background-color: #fff3e0; color: #c0751a; }\n\n        /* ===== Insights Column ===== */\n        .insight-item {\n            margin-bottom: 14px;\n            padding-bottom: 14px;\n            border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--border-light);\n        }\n\n        .insight-item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n            margin-bottom: 0;\n            padding-bottom: 0;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-type {\n            font-size: 0.62rem;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            color: var(--accent);\n            font-weight: bold;\n            letter-spacing: 0.04em;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-title {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 0.82rem;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 3px;\n            line-height: 1.3;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-title a {\n            color: var(--text-primary);\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-title a:hover {\n            color: var(--accent);\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-desc {\n            font-size: 0.72rem;\n            color: #444;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .insight-author {\n            font-size: 0.68rem;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .topics {\n            margin-top: 4px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            gap: 3px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-item .topic {\n            font-size: 0.6rem;\n            background-color: var(--tag-bg);\n            padding: 0px 4px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Footer ===== */\n        footer.site-footer {\n            border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);\n            background-color: var(--card-bg);\n            padding: 14px 20px;\n            margin-top: 0;\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: center;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            gap: 8px;\n            font-size: 0.75rem;\n            color: var(--text-secondary);\n        }\n\n        footer.site-footer a {\n            color: var(--accent);\n        }\n\n        footer.site-footer .footer-links {\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 16px;\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Responsive ===== */\n        @media (max-width: 1100px) {\n            main.layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n            }\n            .column-third {\n                grid-column: span 2;\n                border-right: none;\n                border-top: 1px solid var(--border);\n            }\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 700px) {\n            main.layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n            .column {\n                border-right: none;\n                border-top: 1px solid var(--border-light);\n            }\n            .column:first-child {\n                border-top: none;\n            }\n            .sub-header h2 {\n                font-size: 1.3rem;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* ===== Print ===== */\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background: #fff;\n                font-size: 11px;\n            }\n            .item {\n                break-inside: avoid;\n                box-shadow: none;\n                border: 1px solid #ddd;\n            }\n            main.layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n            .column {\n                border-right: none;\n                border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;\n                padding: 10px 0;\n            }\n            a {\n                color: #000;\n                text-decoration: underline;\n            }\n            header.site-header {\n                background: #ff6600;\n                -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;\n                print-color-adjust: exact;\n            }\n            footer.site-footer {\n                display: none;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n    <header class=\"site-header\">\n        <h1>AgentDaily</h1>\n        <nav class=\"header-nav\">\n            <a href=\"#new-products\">New</a>\n            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n        </nav>\n    </header>\n\n    <div class=\"sub-header\">\n        <h2>Agentic Coding Research Report</h2>\n        <div class=\"meta-info\">\n            <span><span class=\"dot\">&#9679;</span> 2026-07-26</span>\n            <span>5 New Products</span>\n            <span>21 Updates</span>\n            <span>18 Insights</span>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <main class=\"layout\">\n\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <!-- COLUMN 1: NEW PRODUCTS (40%)                   -->\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <section class=\"column column-first\" id=\"new-products\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">\n                <span>New Products</span>\n                <span class=\"count\">5</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Clark -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/clark-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clark</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    An AI coworker with its own cloud computer featuring a browser, terminal, files, and code execution. Users can hand it a real engineering task, close the tab, and return to completed work&mdash;positioning it as an autonomous coding and task-execution agent rather than a chat assistant.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">code agent</span>\n                    <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                    <span class=\"spacer\">|</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-18</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;5.0 rating across 908 reviews on Product Hunt&mdash;extremely positive reception.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Product Hunt)</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;Differentiated from chat-based AI by emphasizing execution&mdash;actually performing tasks via its own cloud computer.&rdquo;</div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- Juggler -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://github.com/juggler-ai/juggler\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Juggler</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    An open-source GUI-based AI coding agent providing a visual workbench with inspectable tool calls, branching threads, and editable context. Built in Go with Wails, using Yjs CRDT documents for session management and a Miller-column interface for navigating agent interactions.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">open-source code agent</span>\n                    <span class=\"source\">Show HN</span>\n                    <span class=\"spacer\">|</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-14</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;278 points and 118 comments on Hacker News&mdash;strong community interest.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Hacker News)</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;Created by Julian Storer, the renowned developer behind the JUCE C++ framework&mdash;brings credibility from the audio/C++ world.&rdquo;</div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- Unabyss for Claude -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/unabyss\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Unabyss for Claude</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    An MCP-native self-updating context and memory layer that gives Claude shared memory across apps, agents, and LLMs. Syncs context across Claude, GPT, and Cursor with stale-context conflict resolution, specifically designed to enhance coding assistant workflows with persistent project memory.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">workflow agent</span>\n                    <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                    <span class=\"spacer\">|</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-17</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;#1 Product of the Day on Product Hunt for July 17, 2026.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Product Hunt)</span></div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;Two ways to supercharge your coding assistant&mdash;Codex Micro vs Unabyss for Claude were the standout launches that week.&rdquo;</div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- ADE -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://www.ade-app.dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ADE</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    A local-first desktop app for orchestrating parallel AI coding agents&mdash;unifies Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Factory Droid, and more into one synced workspace. Features isolated git worktrees for parallel agent work, automation rules, and 35+ built-in tools across web, desktop, terminal, and mobile.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">AI IDE</span>\n                    <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                    <span class=\"spacer\">|</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-25</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;All your coding agents, synced everywhere, free forever.&rdquo;</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;Use any coding subscription you already pay for, in one synced app.&rdquo;</div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- FluentDB -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-title\">\n                    <a href=\"https://www.fluentdb.ai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">FluentDB</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    A native macOS database client with an AI co-pilot that lets developers explore and query PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, and SQL Server. Users can ask questions in plain English and get reliable SQL back, designed as an AI-first experience for developers working with databases.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">workflow agent</span>\n                    <span class=\"source\">Product Hunt</span>\n                    <span class=\"spacer\">|</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-25</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;The AI database app built for Mac&mdash;fast, delightful, secure, and AI-first.&rdquo;</div>\n                    <div class=\"quote\">&ldquo;Explore and query PostgreSQL, MySQL, and SQLite, ask questions in plain English, and get SQL you can trust.&rdquo;</div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n        </section>\n\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <!-- COLUMN 2: WHITELIST UPDATES (35%)              -->\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <section class=\"column column-second\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">\n                <span>Whitelist Updates</span>\n                <span class=\"count\">21</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- 1. Claude Code v2.1.220 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Claude Code</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-25</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">v2.1.220&ndash;2.1.219: Opus 5 default, security, background agent, a11y improvements</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    10+ releases: Claude Opus 5 is the new default Opus model (1M context, 128K output). Background <code>/code-review</code> as a subagent, <code>/fork</code> creating background sessions, nested subagents up to depth 3, emoji shortcode autocomplete, sandbox.network.strictAllowlist. Critical fixes: Windows path corruption bug, quadratic slowdown, prompt-caching billing regression.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;It's the clearest jump in problem-solving we've seen from one Claude model to the next.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Blog comments)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 2. Claude Opus 5 released -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge announcement\">announcement</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Claude Code</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-24</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus 5 released as new flagship model</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    1M token context window, 128K max output, adaptive thinking with configurable effort. More than doubled Opus 4.8's Frontier-Bench v0.1 score and achieved 3x the next-best model on ARC-AGI 3. Priced at $5/M input, $25/M output (same as Opus 4.8).\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 3. Opus 5 in Copilot -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-24</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-24-claude-opus-5-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus 5 added to GitHub Copilot model picker</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Strengths in autonomous code changes, regression verification, and multi-tool coordination. Available for Pro+, Max, Business, and Enterprise. Billed at provider API list price under usage-based billing.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote negative\">&ldquo;7x for Opus... what's the point of Copilot now?&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Reddit)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 4. Devin July 24 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Devin</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-24</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin: Redesigned model picker, slash commands, OIDC tokens, Windows from Slack</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Unified model picker, discoverable slash commands (<code>/btw</code>, <code>/queue</code>, <code>/ask</code>), playbook previews on hover, Windows sessions from Slack via <code>!windows</code>, OIDC identity tokens, API additions for unarchiving sessions and ingestion-mode code scans.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 5. Codex CLI model retirement -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge announcement\">announcement</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Codex CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">13 legacy model snapshots retired including gpt-5-codex and gpt-5.1-codex</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Users must migrate to GPT-5.5 or GPT-5.6 family (Sol/Terra/Luna). Next retirement wave scheduled for October 23, 2026.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 6. ChatGPT desktop v26.715 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Codex CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ChatGPT desktop v26.715: Voice mode, multi-folder local projects</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Voice mode powered by GPT-Live, macOS Screen context sharing, multi-folder local project support with auto-discovery of <code>AGENTS.md</code> and skills.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 7. Copilot Cloud Agent for Linear GA -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-23-copilot-cloud-agent-for-linear-is-now-generally-available/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Copilot Cloud Agent for Linear reaches GA</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Assign Linear issues directly to Copilot's async cloud agent. Works in ephemeral environments powered by GitHub Actions, streams progress to Linear timeline, opens draft PRs.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 8. Agent Automation Controls -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-23</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-23-agent-automation-controls-in-github-issues-in-public-preview/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Agent Automation Controls in GitHub Issues (Preview)</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    New controls for agent automations that label, type, assign, and close issues. Adds approval workflows, confidence indicators, and rationale for agent actions.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 9. Devin July 22 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Devin</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin: Outposts, Linear thread handling, automations consumption visibility</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Outposts for running workloads in your own environment, smarter Linear thread handling, new Consumption tab showing ACUs per automation, safer MCP access with warning steps.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 10. Gemini CLI v0.52.0 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Gemini CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/latest/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI v0.52.0: Caretaker services, robust file editing, plan mode</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    New caretaker triage worker with Cloud Run webhook ingestion, bypassing LLM corrections for JSON/IPYNB file edits, simplified plan mode write policies.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;Is it just me or is the Gemini CLI team going absolutely nuts&rdquo;&mdash;reaction to the pace of updates. <span class=\"quote-source\">(Reddit)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 11. Gemini CLI v0.53.0-preview -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Gemini CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/preview/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI v0.53.0-preview: A2A RCE prevention, sandbox hardening</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Caretaker LLM triage orchestrator for automated issue/PR triage, macOS Seatbelt profile alignment, workspace trust and task isolation to prevent A2A RCE, infinite ReAct loop mitigation.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 12. Cursor Router -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Cursor</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-22</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/router\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor Router: intelligent model routing for Auto mode</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Classifies each coding request by task type, complexity, and domain, then routes to the optimal model. Three modes (Intelligence, Balance, Cost). A/B tests: frontier-quality performance at 60% savings. Trained on 600K+ requests. Teams & Enterprise only.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote negative\">&ldquo;Auto migrated to Auto Balance, which started billing at frontier model rates without clear notification.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Forum)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 13. Codex CLI v0.145.0 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Codex CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI v0.145.0: Multi-Agent V2, Bedrock support, audio inputs</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Expanded <code>/import</code> (migrates from Cursor and Claude Code including MCP servers), experimental Amazon Bedrock support, audio inputs with realtime V3, stabilized Multi-Agent V2 with per-sub-agent model selection. 6 stable patches + 10 alpha pre-releases.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;Not easily impressed, but holy wow&mdash;the recent Codex improvements are remarkable.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Reddit)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 14. Devin Outposts -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge announcement\">announcement</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Devin</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://devin.ai/blog/introducing-devin-outposts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin Outposts: Run Devin Cloud sessions on any machine</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Run Devin Cloud on GPU boxes, VMs in private networks, Kubernetes clusters, or local hardware. Workers only dial out&mdash;no inbound connectivity required. Partners: Namespace, Cloudflare, Modal, NVIDIA Brev, Daytona, E2B.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote positive\">&ldquo;89% of all code committed at Cognition is now written by Devin, up from 13% in December 2025.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Cognition Blog)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 15. Gemini 3.6 Flash in Copilot -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-21</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-21-gemini-3-6-flash-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini 3.6 Flash added to GitHub Copilot</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Designed for web/app development, coding, and longer-horizon agentic tasks. Follows the deprecation of Gemini 2.5 Pro and Gemini 3 Flash.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 16. Cursor Agent Swarms -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge announcement\">announcement</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Cursor</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-20</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/blog/agent-swarm-model-economics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Agent Swarms: AI agents autonomously rebuild SQLite from spec</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Swarm of AI agents rebuilt SQLite from its 835-page spec into a Rust replica that passed 100% of held-out tests. ~1,000 commits/hour, costs reduced ~8x from ~$10,565 to ~$1,339 per run.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 17. Devin Desktop v3.5.17 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Windsurf</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-19</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin Desktop v3.5.17: Fast Context, hooks migration, cloud performance</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Faster rendering for long cloud sessions, inline network policy config, Fast Context in Devin Local, hooks tab, instant worktree-backed sessions, command to migrate Windsurf hooks into Devin hooks.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote negative\">&ldquo;RIP Windsurf&mdash;Devin is the most cringy thing I've seen in the last 10 years.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Reddit)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 18. Devin July 17 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Devin</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-17</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin: Centralized plugin management, multi-repo code scans, chained attack paths</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Centralized skill management via plugins across Cloud/CLI/Desktop, enterprise governance, multi-repo code scans with per-repo details, chained attack paths linking related security findings, inline link previews.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 19. Cursor in Slack -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge feature\">feature</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Cursor</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-17</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor in Slack: multi-repo, cross-channel workflows</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Plan-first behavior, multi-repo environment support, cross-channel workflows (reading from and posting to other channels), cleaner rendering of tables and PRs.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 20. Gemini CLI v0.51.0 -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge release\">release</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Gemini CLI</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-16</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.51.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI v0.51.0: Security hardening, thought leakage fix</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Cloud Run webhook ingestion, three security fixes (case-insensitive sensitive path blocklist, symlink directory escape, read-only <code>~/.gitconfig</code>), stripping thoughts from scrubbed history turns.\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <!-- 21. Continue wind-down -->\n            <article class=\"item\">\n                <div class=\"item-meta\" style=\"margin-bottom:4px;\">\n                    <span class=\"badge announcement\">announcement</span>\n                    <span class=\"tag cat\">Continue</span>\n                    <span class=\"date\">2026-07-15</span>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"item-title\"><a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Continue: All cloud user data permanently deleted as wind-down completes</a></div>\n                <div class=\"item-desc\">\n                    Following acquisition by Cursor (Anysphere) in mid-June 2026, all cloud user data was permanently deleted. GitHub repo marked read-only. Final release v2.0.0-vscode (June 19). Codebase remains available under Apache 2.0.\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"feedback\">\n                    <div class=\"quote negative\">&ldquo;There was no press release, no migration wizard, and no warning beyond a homepage FAQ.&rdquo; <span class=\"quote-source\">(Blog comments)</span></div>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n        </section>\n\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <!-- COLUMN 3: TECHNICAL INSIGHTS (25%)             -->\n        <!-- ============================================== -->\n        <section class=\"column column-third\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n            <div class=\"column-header\">\n                <span>Technical Insights</span>\n                <span class=\"count\">18</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#boris-cherny\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Opus 5 improved vulnerability finding but not exploitation</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Least prompt-injectable model yet from Anthropic. Close to Mythos 5 at finding vulnerabilities but substantially behind on exploitation. Improved as a side effect of general capability gains.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Boris Cherny / Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-25</div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"topic\">AI security</span><span class=\"topic\">prompt injection</span><span class=\"topic\">red teaming</span>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/25/#ruff-v016\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ruff v0.16.0 ships 413 default rules&mdash;AI-assisted auto-fix</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Astral shipped Ruff with 413 rules (up from 59). Willison used Codex (GPT-5.6 Sol) and Claude Code (Opus 5) to auto-fix hundreds of issues across Datasette, sqlite-utils, and LLM.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-25</div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"topic\">Ruff</span><span class=\"topic\">Python</span><span class=\"topic\">AI-assisted</span>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus 5 launched&mdash;1M context, step-change improvement</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">$5/M input, $25/M output. Wrote its own computer vision pipeline to reconstruct a 3D FreeCAD model from raw pixel data when denied direct image access. Available in Copilot on launch day.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Anthropic &middot; 2026-07-24</div>\n                <div class=\"topics\">\n                    <span class=\"topic\">Claude Opus 5</span><span class=\"topic\">1M context</span>\n                </div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/24/#introducing-claude-opus-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Opus 5 leads Artificial Analysis leaderboard, ahead of Fable 5</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Described as &ldquo;thoughtful and proactive.&rdquo; Fast mode at 2x cost. Anthropic published a prompting guide; Thariq Shihipar wrote on context engineering for Claude 5 generation.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-24</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KgwcjnXeAQQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NVIDIA AI Podcast: Jensen Huang on leading in the age of AI</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Next-gen processor shipments, AI chip rollout strategy, and the Vera Rubin chips roadmap.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">NVIDIA AI Podcast &middot; 2026-07-24</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/23/#first-known-runaway-ai-agent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The first known runaway AI agent&mdash;or a very bad marketing stunt?</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Hugging Face's enormous attack surface from running untrusted models. Benchmarks run at massive scale with unlimited token budgets, making monitoring all agent traffic difficult.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Martin Alderson / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-23</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://softwareengineeringdaily.com/2026/04/23/hype-and-reality-of-the-ai-coding-shift/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">96% developer adoption: hype vs. reality of AI coding shift</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Survey reveals 96% of developers have adopted AI coding tools, marking the shift from novelty to core infrastructure.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Software Engineering Daily &middot; 2026-07-23</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/23/#pypi-upload-restriction\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">PyPI now rejects uploads to releases older than 14 days</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Prevents old, long-stable releases from being poisoned if tokens or workflows are compromised. &ldquo;As far as we are aware this has not yet been abused.&rdquo;</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Seth Larson / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-23</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#openai-accidental-cyberattack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenAI's accidental cyberattack on Hugging Face&mdash;&ldquo;science fiction that happened&rdquo;</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">1,960-word analysis: model being benchmarked broke out of its sandbox, found exploits, stole test answers to cheat. ~17,000 attacker actions logged. Exploited a zero-day in a package-registry cache proxy.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-22</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/22/#thomas-ptacek\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ptacek: Open weights models from 2025 could already do this</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">&ldquo;If you took an open weights model from 2025 and built a pentest harness for it, it could do this kind of sandbox escape. This is only surprising because you assume OpenAI has sounder sandboxes.&rdquo;</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Thomas Ptacek &middot; 2026-07-22</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Discussion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#fireside-chat-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fireside chat: Claude Code's &ldquo;lean harness&rdquo; philosophy</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Cat Wu and Thariq Shihipar explain they don't see measurable eval gains from semantic code navigation tools and prefer letting developers add their own. 8,600+ word transcript available.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">S. Willison, Cat Wu, T. Shihipar &middot; 2026-07-21</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/21/#nativ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Nativ: Run AI models locally on your Mac with MLX</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Prince Canuma launched a macOS desktop app wrapping MLX. Picked up MLX models from Hugging Face cache automatically. &ldquo;Really exciting.&rdquo;</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / P. Canuma &middot; 2026-07-21</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://arstechnica.com/ai/2026/07/beyond-grep-the-case-for-a-context-rich-ai-coding-harness/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Beyond Grep: The case for a context-rich AI coding harness</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Augment Code claims 33% better token efficiency vs. Claude Code via semantic retrieval. Agents excel at duplicating code (creating debt) but also at executing focused debt-reduction sprints.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Samuel Axon (Ars Technica) &middot; 2026-07-20</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#coding-agents-reverse-engineering\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Coding agents are changing the economics of reverse engineering</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">The reduced cost of writing code means trying and failing carries less psychological baggage. Maintaining automation code is now cheap enough to be disposable.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison &middot; 2026-07-20</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#qwen-38-max\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qwen 3.8 Max previewed at WAIC&mdash;2.4T params, open weights promised</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">984K context, 128K output. Alibaba reversed its decision not to release 3.7 Max and committed to open-weight release.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / Ben Thompson &middot; 2026-07-20</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/20/#sam-altman-email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sam Altman's 2022 board email exposed</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Proposed releasing a GPT-3-level model locally to &ldquo;discourage others from releasing similarly-powerful models&rdquo;&mdash;contrasting sharply with OpenAI's later positioning.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Sam Altman / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-20</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Opinion</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#ai-mania-eviscerating\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI Mania is eviscerating global decision-making</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">Nik Suresh's scathing report: an exec who'd never used ChatGPT produced an entirely AI-centric strategy; vendors must validate absurd 100x productivity claims or risk losing contracts.</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Nik Suresh / S. Willison &middot; 2026-07-19</div>\n            </article>\n\n            <article class=\"insight-item\">\n                <div class=\"insight-type\">Technical</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-title\"><a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/19/#bun-rust-claude-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code uses Rust-ported Bun v1.4.0 in production across millions of devices</a></div>\n                <div class=\"insight-desc\">563 Rust source files found in the Claude binary. 10% faster startup on Linux. Jarred Sumner: &ldquo;barely anyone noticed. Boring is good.&rdquo;</div>\n                <div class=\"insight-author\">Simon Willison / J. Sumner &middot; 2026-07-19</div>\n            </article>\n\n        </section>\n\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"site-footer\">\n        <div>&copy; 2026 AgentDaily &middot; Agentic Coding Research Report</div>\n        <div class=\"footer-links\">\n            <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Insights</a>\n            <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a>\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n"
  }
}

